	// ApikeyRevokeWithBody Revoke the calling API key
	//
	// Permanently revokes **the key making this call**, nothing else: a key can only revoke itself, so this cannot be used to change any other key. Use it when an agent or script is finished, or suspects its key has leaked. Any key can call it, including a read-only one.
