// - `addedAfter` / `addedBefore` — when the domain joined this account at Porkbun, by registration or transfer (`addedDate`). Use `addedAfter` to fetch only what's new since your last sync
// - `createdAfter` / `createdBefore` — the registry creation date (`createDate`); a transferred-in domain keeps its original one
// - `expiresAfter` / `expiresBefore` — an expiry window by date
// - `autoRenew` — `yes` / `no`
// - `apiAccess` — `yes` / `no` (filter to domains the API key can operate on)
// - `sortName` — `domain` / `tld` / `create_date` / `added_date` / `expire_date`
//
// Dates are `YYYY-MM-DD` or `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`, in UTC like every date in the response. `...After` includes the moment given; `...Before` excludes it.
// - `sortDirection` — `asc` / `desc`
//
// Supports both GET (with header auth) and POST (with body or header auth). For multi-value `tlds` on GET, use bracket syntax: `?tlds[]=com&tlds[]=io`.
